SECraft — Master Implementation Prompt
Product Repositioning, UX, Learning Architecture, Accounts, Backend, Security & Platform Integration

IMPORTANT: This is an implementation task against an existing repository.

Do not start by rebuilding, replacing, or restructuring the application.

First inspect the complete existing repository, understand how the current application works, compare it against this specification, identify conflicts/gaps, and then implement the changes incrementally.

The existing working application, learning content, visual identity, animations, local-first behavior, GitHub Pages deployment, and useful functionality are valuable assets and must be preserved unless this specification explicitly requires a change.

1. PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Evolve the existing WiFiForge/SecCraft application into a broader cybersecurity learning platform called SecCraft.

SecCraft should become a platform for practical, evidence-led cybersecurity learning.

The current Wireless Pentesting content becomes:

Learning Path #1 — Wireless Pentesting

The architecture must be generic enough to support future learning paths such as Web, API, Android, Network, Active Directory, Cloud, AI/LLM Security, Blue Team/SOC, etc., without implementing those future paths now.

Do not make the backend, routing, database, or UI fundamentally Wireless-specific.

