21. EXISTING BACKEND SECURITY ISSUES — DO NOT CARRY THEM FORWARD

The current repository audit found that the existing optional API is not safe to expose as a multi-user service.

Known issues include:

shared "local" user ID
unauthenticated progress endpoints
unauthenticated PCAP upload
upload body read before size validation
no explicit parser timeout
demo JWT rather than real account ownership
wildcard CORS methods/headers
rate limiting dependent on Nginx
exposed FastAPI documentation
current API not connected to the published account model

Therefore:

Do not simply expose the existing API. Replace/adapt its authentication and ownership model as part of the migration.

The repository audit explicitly identifies this as a deployment blocker for a multi-user API.

