37. IMPLEMENTATION RULES
Rule 1 — Inspect first

Never modify unfamiliar architecture blindly.

Rule 2 — Reuse before rebuilding

If an existing component solves the problem, extend it.

Rule 3 — One source of truth

Do not create competing:

progress stores
API clients
routing systems
auth systems
XP engines
content registries
Rule 4 — No fake functionality

Do not create buttons, dashboards, analytics or settings that do not have real underlying behavior.

Rule 5 — No premature abstraction

Do not build infrastructure for future paths that does not currently have a concrete requirement.

Rule 6 — Preserve guest mode

Account infrastructure must not unnecessarily destroy local learning.

Rule 7 — Security server-side

Frontend guards are UX.

Backend authorization is security.

Rule 8 — Do not expose secrets

Never put privileged credentials into frontend code.

Rule 9 — Do not silently change product behavior

If a change affects existing learning behavior, assess regression impact first.

Rule 10 — Do not create conflicting architecture

The target architecture is:

React/Vite
+
Supabase Auth
+
FastAPI
+
PostgreSQL

Do not introduce another authentication provider, another backend framework, another database strategy, or another competing persistence architecture without a concrete repository-derived reason.

